# The Next Chapter
#
# A score for a film about a life being lived: dawn on the sea, an old tree with a family under it,
# a kite on a windy hill, a coast road running on toward a lighthouse, a harbour lighting up at
# dusk, and a path in the morning. D major at 88, six scenes of five bars that each land on a
# downbeat, then a held D add9.
#
# It is played on the analog voices. The bed is tungsten: two drifting cards of pulse and saw
# with slow PWM, its ladder opening with the dawn, closing in the harbour, blooming in the morning.
# The tune is the Wurlitzer (wurly). On the road and in the morning the line is sung by
# heliograph, the hard-synced vocal lead, gliding between notes. The arpeggio is peppermint,
# a bright pluck whose resonant filter sweeps open through the kite and the road. Under it all
# sunbass and a light 909; the music box and bells only for light.

bpm 88
gate 0.9
tail 5

section DAWN     0..20
section TREE     20..40
section KITE     40..60
section ROAD     60..80
section HARBOUR  80..100
section MORNING  100..120
section YOURS    120..132

automate bpm
88 R:120 70:12@smooth
automate reverb_decay
0.55
automate reverb_wet
0.17
automate chorus_mode
0
automate spring
0.04
automate tape_wow
0.05
automate tape_flutter
0.03
automate tape_drive
0.08
automate tape_age
0.06

# ------------------------------------------------ the bed: tungsten, the ladder opening with the light
track bed vel=0.3 len=4 patch=tungsten reverb_send=0.22 pan=-0.08
[57 62 66]@0.3 [57 61 64]@0.3 [54 59 62]@0.3 [55 59 62]@0.3 [57 62 64]@0.3
